---
<%#- Declaring a version asserts that this tree was checked against that
     release of the OKF spec, which is an obligation and not just a label:
     a future OKF release makes the claim stale until someone re-verifies
     the tree and bumps this literal here and in both fixture trees'
     `index.md`. Quoted because unquoted it is a YAML float, and a float
     cannot carry a version: `0.10` and `0.1` both load as 0.1, so the
     day OKF reaches 0.10 the declaration silently claims 0.1. Dropping
     the key instead was rejected: §12 makes it optional, but a consumer
     that cannot tell which spec version produced a tree has to guess, and
     the whole point of conforming is to spare it that. See
     docs/adr/0005-okf-bundle-conformance.md. -%>
okf_version: "0.2"
---

